# The CPU guard (app/drums/cpuguard.h) on the host's clock, as on the FM-1. Under the host's own load (far under a
# block's 5.8 ms) it never steps. Then a forced overload: "heavy 1000" makes each block take 1 ms a sounding voice
# (the first song's 6 or so: past its 5.8 ms), so the guard climbs the whole ladder while the song plays on, loud;
# stopped, it comes back down a level at a time after 20 s of calm. (Which voices it cuts is song_test's
# test_guard_voices: these held chords have no release tails to cut.) Writes guard.wav.
#   app/build/host/vnl-1_host tests/scenarios/guard.vnl app/build/scenarios
wav guard.wav
master 4096
heavy 0
tap PLAY
wait 10000
expect playing 1
expect guard 0
heavy 1000
wait 8000
# up the ladder, a level at a time, to the top
expect guard_top 5
peakreset
wait 4000
expect playing 1
expect peak_db_min -20
# stopped: calm, so the levels come off, the first after 20 s, then one each 2 s
tap PLAY
wait 15000
expect guard 5
wait 21000
expect guard 0
expect guard_recov 5
heavy 0 off
wavstop
